Implementation of AI-Based Algorithms for Robotic Path Planning

This project aims to develop and implement AI-based algorithms to enhance path planning for robotic systems. The intern will design and refine algorithms that enable robots to navigate complex environments efficiently, avoiding obstacles and optimizing routes to achieve target destinations. Key components of the project include exploring AI techniques such as reinforcement learning, genetic algorithms, and neural networks to improve decision-making capabilities. The intern will also test and validate these algorithms in simulated and real-world scenarios to ensure reliability and scalability. The objective is to advance robotic autonomy and performance, with applications ranging from warehouse automation to autonomous vehicles.
